<title>USA: Digital computer operations post open - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Digital computer operations post open - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Equipment Corp's chief executive officer does not intend to choose someone as head of computer operations, a position which has remained vacant since July, the Wall Street Journal reported Friday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said Robert Palmer told employees in an internal memorandum that he did not plan to name a successor to Enrico Pesatori, who resigned from the second most important post in the company last July.</p>
<p>Palmer has since been working as acting head of operations, it added.</p>
</text>
